<component type="console-application">
  <id>io.spt.spt</id>
  <name>spt</name>
  <summary>Permanent SSH and SSH3 tunnels with reconnect and service integration</summary>

  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>

  <developer_name>Mariana</developer_name>

  <description>
    <p>
      spt establishes and maintains permanent SSH tunnels: local and reverse
      port forwards that survive network drops, host restarts, service
      restarts, DNS changes, and ordinary operational drift.
    </p>
    <p>
      Transports and forwards:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>SSH2 transport via libssh2 and an experimental SSH3 transport over QUIC and HTTP/3.</li>
      <li>Local and remote TCP forwards; UDP forwards over SSH3.</li>
      <li>Built-in transparent DNS resolver with split-horizon and SRV synthesis.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Operational surface:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Encrypted secret vault (AES-256-GCM with Argon2id) and OS keychain integration.</li>
      <li>Service integration for systemd, launchd, the Windows SCM, OpenRC, SysV, and Task Scheduler.</li>
      <li>Structured observability via tracing, OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, and SNMP.</li>
      <li>Embedded MCP server and a TUI configurator.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      spt is client-only: it connects to existing SSH or SSH3 servers and
      maintains forwards through them. The Flathub build is the standard
      Linux distribution channel; native packages are also published for
      Homebrew, Scoop, Winget, Chocolatey, and Snap.
    </p>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.spt.spt.desktop</launchable>

  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/supermarsx/ssh-perma-tunnel</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/supermarsx/ssh-perma-tunnel/issues</url>
